          "heading": "Macs Page taken off on oxygen after head hit against Stormers",
          "body": "Scarlets winger Macs Page, uncapped and left out of Steve Tandy's 39-man autumn squad, was forced off in Cape Town after his head hit the turf in the United Rugby Championship clash with the Stormers. He appeared to lose consciousness as he spilled the ball forward, and a stretcher was brought on before he walked off on oxygen. Page had already dotted down for his fifth try of the season. Scarlets' Nigel Davies had said it was only a matter of time before Wales brought him in."
